        "body": "Description\r\n\r\nAdds a link to the \"Implicit solvent calculations using Qiskit Serverless\" tutorial in the documentation's Tutorials section, underneath the two tutorials already listed there. This was requested by @jenglick in the linked issue.\r\n\r\nFixes #376\r\n\r\nHow Has This Been Tested?\r\n\r\nThis is a documentation-only change to docs/index.rst, one new line is added to the existing toctree block under the Tutorials caption. Verified that the added line matches the indentation and formatting of the two existing tutorial entries, that the link text matches the tutorial's actual page title, and that the URL resolves correctly.\r\n\r\n(no additional tests as no code was changed)\r\n\r\nTest Configuration:\r\n\r\nPython version: N/A\r\nOperating system and system architecture: N/A\r\nChecklist:\r\n  [x] My code follows the style guidelines of this project\r\n  [x] I have performed a self-review of my own code\r\n  [ ] I have commented my code, particularly in hard-to-understand areas\r\n  [x] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation\r\n  [x] My changes generate no new errors or warnings\r\n  [ ] My code and tests pass locally and have at least 80% line coverage\r\n  [x] Any dependent changes have been merged and published in downstream modules\r\n  [x] All AI-generated changes have been thoroughly human reviewed and checked",
